      "headline": "Tightening Your Focus: The Two Parts of You",
      "keyInsight": "The secret to ending an addiction is shockingly simple: divide and conquer. Your mind contains your true voice, but it also carries an ancient appetite machine. That primitive center cannot reason, plan for tomorrow, or buy groceries. It only knows how to demand immediate pleasure. When you feel a sudden craving, it cleverly disguises itself in the first person. It says, 'I need a drink right now to relax.' Notice the trap? It pretended to be you. The moment you catch that trick, the power flips instantly. It is not 'I want this.' It is 'That beastly appetite wants this.' You tighten your focus like a camera lens. Suddenly, the monster loses its disguise and shrinks into background static.",
